,{"surface":"வேண்டின்","parts":[{"text":"வேண்டு","lemma":"vēṇṭu","gloss":"want"},{"text":"இன்","lemma":"iṉ","gloss":"if"}],"gloss":"if you want"},{"surface":"எம்மொடு","parts":[{"text":"எம்","lemma":"em","gloss":"us"},{"text":"ஒடு","lemma":"oṭu","gloss":"with"}],"gloss":"with us"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"நீயும்","parts":[{"text":"நீ","lemma":"nī","gloss":"you"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"um","gloss":"also"}],"gloss":"you also"},{"surface":"வம்மோ","parts":[{"text":"வம்மோ","lemma":"வம்மோ","gloss":"please come"}],"gloss":"please come","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"முதுவாய்","parts":[{"text":"முது","lemma":"mutu","gloss":"wise"},{"text":"வாய்","lemma":"vāy","gloss":"tongue/mouth"}],"gloss":"wise-tongued"},{"surface":"இரவல","parts":[{"text":"இரவல","lemma":"இரவல","gloss":"O suppliant!"}],"gloss":"O suppliant!","split_unverified":true}]},{"words":[{"surface":"யாம்","parts":[{"text":"யாம்","lemma":"yām","gloss":"we"}],"gloss":"we"},{"surface":"தன்","parts":[{"text":"தன்","lemma":"taṉ","gloss":"his"}],"gloss":"his"},{"surface":"இரக்கும்","parts":[{"text":"இரக்கும்","lemma":"இரக்கும்","gloss":"begging"}],"gloss":"begging","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"காலை","parts":[{"text":"காலை","lemma":"kālai","gloss":"time"}],"gloss":"time"},{"surface":"தான்","parts":[{"text":"தான்","lemma":"tāṉ","gloss":"he himself"}],"gloss":"he himself"},{"surface":"எம்","parts":[{"text":"எம்","lemma":"em","gloss":"our"}],"gloss":"our"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"உண்ணா","parts":[{"text":"உண்","lemma":"uṇ","gloss":"eat"},{"text":"ஆ","lemma":"ā","gloss":"negative relative participle"}],"gloss":"unfed"},{"surface":"மருங்குல்","parts":[{"text":"மருங்குல்","lemma":"maruṅkul","gloss":"stomach/waist"}],"gloss":"stomach"},{"surface":"காட்டி","parts":[{"text":"காட்டு","lemma":"kāṭṭu","gloss":"show"},{"text":"இ","lemma":"i","gloss":"having"}],"gloss":"having shown"},{"surface":"தன்","parts":[{"text":"தன்","lemma":"taṉ","gloss":"his"}],"gloss":"his"},{"surface":"ஊர்","parts":[{"text":"ஊர்","lemma":"ūr","gloss":"town"}],"gloss":"town"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"கருங்கை","parts":[{"text":"கருங்கை","lemma":"கருங்கை","gloss":"strong-handed"}],"gloss":"strong-handed","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"கொல்லனை","parts":[{"text":"கொல்லன்","lemma":"kollaṉ","gloss":"blacksmith"},{"text":"ஐ","lemma":"ai","gloss":"accusative suffix"}],"gloss":"blacksmith"},{"surface":"இரக்கும்","parts":[{"text":"இரக்கும்","lemma":"இரக்கும்","gloss":"will beg"}],"gloss":"will beg","split_unverified":true}]},{"words":[{"surface":"திருந்து","parts":[{"text":"திருந்து","lemma":"tiruntu","gloss":"perfect"}],"gloss":"perfect"},{"surface":"இலை","parts":[{"text":"இலை","lemma":"ilai","gloss":"blade/leaf"}],"gloss":"blade"},{"surface":"நெடு","parts":[{"text":"நெடு","lemma":"neṭu","gloss":"long"}],"gloss":"long"},{"surface":"வேல்","parts":[{"text":"வேல்","lemma":"vēl","gloss":"spear"}],"gloss":"spear"},{"surface":"வடித்திசின்","parts":[{"text":"வடி","lemma":"vaṭi","gloss":"forge/shape"},{"text":"திசின்","lemma":"ticiṉ","gloss":"imperative/optative suffix"}],"gloss":"please forge"},{"surface":"எனவே","parts":[{"text":"என","lemma":"eṉa","gloss":"saying"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ē","gloss":"emphasis"}],"gloss":"saying thus indeed"}]}],"literal":"He does not have the wealth to give without satisfying completely / He does not have the baseness of refusing saying 'there is nothing' / Bearing the distress that befell his king, in the battlefield / healing from the painful glorious wounds received from tasting iron weapons / with sword scars mingled like a tree from which medicine is taken / he of the well-formed body without blemishes, welcoming giving / is the lord of Īrntūr, the enemy of the bards' hunger! / If you want your poverty to end, along with us / you also come, O wise-tongued suppliant! / When we beg of him, he himself, showing our / unfed stomachs, to his town's / strong-handed blacksmith, will beg: / 'Forge a long spear with a perfect blade!' saying thus indeed.","translation":"He does not possess the immense wealth to give and satisfy everyone completely, nor does he have the baseness to say 'I have nothing' and turn people away. Bearing the distress that befell his king, he stood in the battlefield, and though he has healed from the painful, glorious wounds made by tasting iron weapons, his body is crowded with sword scars, looking like a tree from which bark has been stripped for medicine. Yet, with a well-formed body free of moral blemish, he welcomes giving. He is the lord of Īrntūr, the sworn enemy of the bards' hunger! If you wish to put an end to your poverty, come along with us, O wise-tongued suppliant! When we go and beg of him, he will look at our empty, unfed stomachs, and then he himself will go to the strong-handed blacksmith of his town and beg: 'Forge me a long spear with a perfect blade!'","modern":"அனைவருக்கும் நிறைவாகக் கொடுக்கும் அளவுக்கு அவனிடம் பெரும் செல்வம் இல்லை. அதே நேரத்தில், 'இல்லை' என்று கூறி மறுக்கும் இழி குணமும் அவனிடம் இல்லை. தன் அரசனுக்கு நேர்ந்த துன்பத்தைத் தாங்கி, போர்க்களத்தில் இரும்பு ஆயுதங்களால் ஏற்பட்ட விழுப்புண்களின் வலி நீங்கி, மருந்துக்காகப் பட்டை உரிக்கப்பட்ட மரத்தைப் போல வாள் வடுக்கள் நிறைந்த உடம்பைக் கொண்டவன் அவன். குற்றமற்ற, நேர்த்தியான உடலமைப்பைக் கொண்ட அவன், கொடை அளிப்பதையே நோக்கமாகக் கொண்டவன். அவனே ஈர்ந்தூர் தலைவனான தோயன் மாறன்; பாணர்களின் பசிக்கு எதிரி! அறிவுடைய இரவலனே! உனது வறுமை நீங்க வேண்டுமானால், எங்களோடு நீயும் வா. நாம் அவனிடம் சென்று இரக்கும்போது, அவன் நமது பசியால் வாடிய வயிற்றைக் கண்டு, தன் ஊரிலுள்ள வலிமையான கைகளைக் கொண்ட கொல்லனிடம் சென்று, 'எனக்காக ஒரு கூர்மையான நீண்ட வேலை வடித்துத் தா' என்று இரந்து கேட்பான் (அதைக் கொண்டு போரிட்டுப் பொருள் பெற்று நமக்கு வழங்குவான்).","explanation":"A bard who has experienced the generosity of the chieftain Īrntūr Kiḻāṉ Tōyaṉ Māṟaṉ is speaking to another poor, wise-tongued suppliant whom he meets on the way. He invites the other bard to join him in visiting the chieftain to end their poverty. The poem describes Tōyaṉ Māṟaṉ as a brave warrior who does not have vast riches but has an immense heart. His body is covered in battle scars, resembling a tree stripped of its bark for medicine. When bards approach him in hunger, since he has no wealth left, he immediately goes to the village blacksmith to request a new spear so he can go to battle, win spoils, and feed them. The image of the 'medicine tree' beautifully illustrates how the chieftain sacrifices his own body in battle for the welfare of others, just as a tree yields its bark to heal people.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"}}